WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.708 --> 00:00:04.333
So you're planning a trip to see Mount Fuji,
but you're not sure where to start.

00:00:04.791 --> 00:00:05.583
What is there to do?

00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:06.875
How many days do you need?

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:08.541
And how do you even get there?

00:00:08.958 --> 00:00:10.208
Well, I'm here to help.

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:14.333
I recently visited Kawaguchiko, and I'll

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:16.041
walk you through everything
you need to know.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.875
From what to do, where to eat, and how
to go about planning your visit.

00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:23.166
So without further delays,
let's get into it.

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:32.416
From Tokyo, it only takes around 2 hours
to get to Fujikawaguchiko.

00:00:32.916 --> 00:00:35.750
This makes the area ideal for a
day trip or even longer.

00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:40.500
Mount Fuji is bordered by 5 lakes, also
known as the Fuji 5 lakes.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.416
The most developed and popular of
the lakes is Kawaguchiko.

00:00:47.291 --> 00:00:49.375
So how many days do you need
to visit Kawaguchiko?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.541
Since it's not too far from Tokyo,

00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:55.125
Kawaguchiko can be done as either
a day trip or even an

00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:55.791
overnight trip.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:00.416
A day trip is ideal if you're only sticking
to exploring the Kawaguchiko area.

00:01:00.875 --> 00:01:04.750
But personally, I think Kawaguchiko is
best experienced over 2 days.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.708
This gives you more time to explore

00:01:06.708 --> 00:01:09.791
Kawaguchiko in depth and open
the doors for exploring

00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:11.000
other nearby areas.

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:15.916
It also gives you more chances to spot Fuji
since Fuji is notoriously shy at times.

00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:18.166
But more importantly, you'll
have more time

00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:20.625
to relax and explore at a
more leisurely pace.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.291
Either way, you can't go wrong with either
a day trip or a slightly longer visit.

00:01:25.041 --> 00:01:27.125
There are a number of ways to
get to Kawaguchiko,

00:01:27.416 --> 00:01:30.208
such as trains or renting a
car, but I personally

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.333
find the easiest way is via
the expressway bus.

00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:36.250
In a little under 2 hours, you can go

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:40.250
directly from stations such as
Tokyo or Shinjuku to Kawaguchiko.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:43.583
And if the weather is clear, you can
even see Fuji along the way.

00:01:45.625 --> 00:01:47.333
You can reserve seats one
month in advance

00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:50.500
via booking websites such
as highway-buses.jp.

00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:54.541
Let's take a closer look at
the Kawaguchiko area.

00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:56.875
Everything is centered around the

00:01:56.875 --> 00:01:59.125
Kawaguchiko station, which is
where you'll arrive.

00:01:59.791 --> 00:02:02.750
It's the main transportation hub for
buses in the Mount Fuji area.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:08.791
For the best areas to stay
in, I recommend

00:02:08.791 --> 00:02:10.750
staying near the Kawaguchiko
station for most

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:11.500
for most people.

00:02:11.916 --> 00:02:13.625
It's the most convenient in terms of

00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:16.291
transportation, and you'll find
plenty of restaurants and

00:02:16.291 --> 00:02:17.666
accommodations to choose from.

00:02:18.291 --> 00:02:21.916
But if you want the best view of Fuji from
your hotel room, then you'll have to go

00:02:21.916 --> 00:02:23.458
along the northern shores of the lake.

00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:25.708
Just be aware that it's less
convenient since

00:02:25.708 --> 00:02:27.791
it's further away from the
station and you'll

00:02:27.791 --> 00:02:30.041
rely more on buses to get
around, and they

00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:32.708
do tend to get crowded during
peak tourist seasons

00:02:33.125 --> 00:02:35.708
For my visit, I chose a hotel
called Rakuyu.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:40.875
We stayed in a lovely Japanese traditional
room with a view over Lake Kawaguchi.

00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:43.666
The hotel is only a 15-minute
walk from the

00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:46.250
station, which made it a great
base for exploration

00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:47.541
of Kawaguchiko.

