00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:07.416
We begin our first day by exploring

00:04:07.416 --> 00:04:10.541
Kawaguchiko and the nearby area
surrounding the lake.

00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:12.875
To get around, there are
buses that covers

00:04:12.875 --> 00:04:16.333
the surrounding area such
as the Kawaguchiko sightseeing bus, 

00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:19.125
which covers the northern
and eastern shores of Kawaguchiko.

00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:22.583
Just use an IC card when you board,
like any other regular bus.

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:27.416
However, in my opinion, renting a bike is
the best way to explore Kawaguchiko.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:31.208
There are plenty of bike rental shops around
the station, so you can't miss them.

00:04:31.833 --> 00:04:34.291
I recommend spending a little
extra on electric bikes.

00:04:34.708 --> 00:04:38.333
Just make getting up on hills or running
around the lake way easier.

00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:45.458
With our bikes, we begin to make our way
towards the famous Chureito Pagoda.

00:04:48.083 --> 00:04:50.166
But first, we make a quick stop along the

00:04:50.166 --> 00:04:52.125
way at the Honcho Street,

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.750
known for its street view of Mt. Fuji.

00:04:55.333 --> 00:04:58.041
This is a very popular photo spot, and

00:04:58.041 --> 00:05:00.666
unfortunately, due to the amount
of people here trying to

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.708
get their photo, the town had to appoint

00:05:02.708 --> 00:05:05.333
staff here to stop people from
blocking traffic.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.000
So I encourage everyone
who visits here to

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.791
be respectful of the staff and locals and

00:05:10.791 --> 00:05:11.791
don't block traffic.

00:05:14.916 --> 00:05:16.541
There are plenty of other
places where you

00:05:16.541 --> 00:05:19.166
can get a similar view of
Fuji, such as the

00:05:19.166 --> 00:05:21.125
side street that's just a
few minutes away,

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.750
or even this spot, just
nearby Kawaguchiko station,

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.416
all without crowds.

00:05:32.916 --> 00:05:35.833
Next up, we finally arrive
at Chureito Pagoda.

00:05:36.416 --> 00:05:38.000
It's here you can get the classic view of

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.333
the Pagoda with Mt. Fuji
in the background.

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:45.875
It's a very popular spot, and it's a little
bit of a climb to get up to the Pagoda.

00:05:47.083 --> 00:05:48.833
Due to the number of people
here, you could

00:05:48.833 --> 00:05:50.750
sometimes expect to wait a
little while before

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.250
reaching the viewing platform.

00:05:58.166 --> 00:06:01.791
After the Pagoda, we bike back towards
the lake to find some lunch.

00:06:04.333 --> 00:06:08.333
One of my favorite meals during my time
in Kawaguchiko was at Pizzeria Onda.

00:06:08.708 --> 00:06:11.333
They serve legit Neapolitan pizzas, and

00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:13.166
you know the owner takes
his craft seriously

00:06:13.416 --> 00:06:14.958
when he's donning a Napoli shirt.

00:06:21.708 --> 00:06:25.833
The service can be a bit slow when it gets
busy, but the pizzas are so worth it.

00:06:26.458 --> 00:06:29.625
If you love a good pizza, then it's definitely
a place worth checking out.

00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:33.041
After lunch, we take things
a little slower.

00:06:36.291 --> 00:06:38.000
We decide to bike along Lake Kawaguchi,

00:06:38.541 --> 00:06:40.916
stopping wherever we wanted,
especially when there

00:06:40.916 --> 00:06:42.458
was a nice view of Mt. Fuji.

00:06:52.458 --> 00:06:56.333
Biking around the lake was arguably my favorite
part of visiting Kawaguchiko.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.833
There are endless viewpoints
along the shore

00:06:58.833 --> 00:07:01.166
where you can just pull over
and take in the view.

00:07:06.041 --> 00:07:08.666
So if I haven't said it already,
I highly recommend

00:07:08.666 --> 00:07:10.916
renting a bike when
exploring Kawaguchiko.

00:07:16.083 --> 00:07:19.208
If you want to try something a little bit different,
you can even rent one of these

00:07:19.208 --> 00:07:21.916
swan boats and head out onto the lake for

00:07:21.916 --> 00:07:24.500
a more unique experience
of Lake Kawaguchi.

00:07:30.541 --> 00:07:35.166
As we continue to bike along the lake, we make
our way to Oishi Park, a free public

00:07:35.208 --> 00:07:37.458
park on the north shore
of Lake Kawaguchi.

00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:41.500
It's known for its seasonal flower
displays and views of Mt. Fuji.

00:07:42.083 --> 00:07:45.541
I recommend grabbing an ice cream, taking
a walk, and enjoying the scenery.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:55.958
As the sun starts to set, we make our way

00:07:55.958 --> 00:07:58.208
back towards the station to
find some dinner.

00:07:58.541 --> 00:08:01.541
We end up at a restaurant called
Fuji Tempura Itaten.

00:08:01.916 --> 00:08:06.291
As the name implies, a restaurant that specializes
in tempura and fried food items.

00:08:07.958 --> 00:08:09.666
The food here was solid, and it was a

00:08:09.666 --> 00:08:12.166
satisfying way to end our first
day in Kawaguchiko.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.208
On our second day, we head out of the

00:08:28.208 --> 00:08:31.958
Kawaguchiko area and jump on a
bus to Lake Yamanaka, the

00:08:31.958 --> 00:08:33.416
largest of the Fuji 5 lakes.

00:08:36.458 --> 00:08:39.083
The lake has a slightly different feel
compared to Kawaguchiko.

00:08:39.625 --> 00:08:41.625
It's more open and less crowded,

00:08:42.041 --> 00:08:46.041
because of its size you get a wider,
more panoramic view of Mount Fuji.

00:08:50.708 --> 00:08:53.250
The lake is also known as Swan Lake, and

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.791
you'll often see swans hanging
out along the shore.

00:09:07.208 --> 00:09:09.750
For lunch, we stop by at a
cafe called The Park.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:11.958
They're known for their souffle pancakes,

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:14.166
and you get an incredible
view of Mount Fuji

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.000
as a backdrop for your pancakes.

00:09:36.083 --> 00:09:38.541
After lunch, we take the
bus, and continue

00:09:38.541 --> 00:09:41.791
to Oshino Hakkai, a small
village known for

00:09:41.833 --> 00:09:44.958
its eight ponds, all fed by snow
melt for Mount Fuji.

00:09:48.166 --> 00:09:50.666
The water here is incredibly
pure, filtered

00:09:50.666 --> 00:09:53.416
naturally through the layers
of volcanic rock over decades

00:09:54.208 --> 00:09:55.791
Because of that, the ponds are extremely

00:09:55.791 --> 00:09:58.791
clear, with reflections of
Fuji on a clear day.

00:09:59.916 --> 00:10:03.250
The place can't get a bit touristy, but
I think it's still worth a visit.

00:10:09.416 --> 00:10:11.458
We then make our way back 
towards Kawaguchiko,

00:10:11.458 --> 00:10:14.125
for our final meal
before heading back to Tokyo

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.250
Hoto is a hearty noodle soup made with

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.583
thick, flat noodles, almost
like udon, but with a

00:10:21.583 --> 00:10:23.125
softer, more rustic texture.

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:25.458
It's served in a miso-based broth, packed

00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:27.833
with seasonal vegetables like
pumpkin, mushroom,

00:10:28.166 --> 00:10:29.208
carrots, and cabbage.

00:10:29.791 --> 00:10:31.666
There's usually no meat in this
traditional version.

00:10:32.291 --> 00:10:35.875
It's simple, filling, and very much
a countryside-style dish.

00:10:43.041 --> 00:10:45.166
Before leaving Kawaguchiko,
we get a quick shot

00:10:45.166 --> 00:10:47.458
of a Lawson with Mount Fuji
in the background.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.375
This is not the Lawson right next to the station,
which usually is pretty crowded.

00:10:55.208 --> 00:10:58.041
And that wraps up our trip
to Kawaguchiko.

00:10:58.833 --> 00:11:00.291
If you're looking for more
things to do or

00:11:00.291 --> 00:11:02.416
just some other options, here's
a short list.

00:11:03.041 --> 00:11:06.666
The Fuji Panoramic Roadway offers panoramic
views over Kawaguchiko.

00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:09.166
Fuji-Q Highland, if you're
into theme parks,

00:11:10.041 --> 00:11:12.500
Lake Motosu, popular for camping
and stargazing,

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.583
and finally, Kawaguchiko Music
Forest Museum,

00:11:15.958 --> 00:11:18.625
a compact theme park and museum
centered around

00:11:18.625 --> 00:11:20.083
self-playing musical instruments.

00:11:26.208 --> 00:11:26.750
And that's it!

00:11:27.208 --> 00:11:30.625
It's a simple trip, but one of the most
rewarding you can do from Tokyo.

00:11:31.416 --> 00:11:33.208
If you're playing a Japan trip,
I'll definitely

00:11:33.208 --> 00:11:36.000
recommend adding Kawaguchiko
to your itinerary.

00:11:36.583 --> 00:11:38.291
It's a great way to get out of the city

00:11:38.291 --> 00:11:41.041
and enjoy arguably the country's
most iconic landmark.

00:11:41.916 --> 00:11:43.750
I hope this video gave you a good idea on

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:46.250
how to go about planning
a trip to see Mount Fuji.

00:11:46.708 --> 00:11:49.458
If you have any questions, 
leave them in the comments below

00:11:49.458 --> 00:11:50.500
and I'll get back to you.

00:11:51.125 --> 00:11:51.958
Thanks for watching,

00:11:51.958 --> 00:11:52.750
this is Allan.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:55.000
I'll see you guys in the next one.

